{{define "integrated"}}
{{$l := .Lang}}{{$a := .Analysis}}{{$lad := .Analysis.Ladder}}{{$fin := .Analysis.Final}}{{$names := ladderNames}}

<section class="band">
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Pertanyaan yang tidak bisa dijawab halaman PERT{{else}}The question the PERT page cannot answer{{end}}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    {{if eq $l "id"}}Halaman PERT menjawab "berapa peluang selesai tepat waktu" dengan satu anggapan besar: setiap aktivitas meleset secara independen, tidak ada risiko yang terjadi, dan orang selalu tersedia. Sponsor tidak bertanya soal waktu saja; ia bertanya apakah proyek ini selesai tepat waktu <em>dan</em> tepat anggaran. Simulasi di halaman ini menambahkan ketidakpastian lapis demi lapis - setiap lapis adalah efek nyata yang terpisah - lalu menjawab pertanyaan sponsor lewat Joint Confidence Level.{{else}}The PERT page answers "what are the odds of finishing on time" under one big assumption: every activity misses independently, no risk ever fires, and people are always available. A sponsor does not ask about time alone; they ask whether the project lands on time <em>and</em> on budget. The simulation on this page adds uncertainty layer by layer - each layer a separate real effect - and answers the sponsor's question through a Joint Confidence Level.{{end}}
  </p>
  <div class="layer-grid">
    {{range $i, $r := $lad}}
    <article class="layer-card l{{$i}}">
      <span class="layer-code">L{{$i}}</span>
      <h3>{{tx (index $names $i) $l}}</h3>
      <p>
        {{if eq $i 0}}{{if eq $l "id"}}Durasi setiap aktivitas diambil acak dari sebaran beta-PERT-nya sendiri-sendiri. Identik dengan halaman PERT.{{else}}Each activity duration is drawn from its own beta-PERT distribution. Identical to the PERT page.{{end}}{{end}}
        {{if eq $i 1}}{{if eq $l "id"}}Aktivitas yang dikerjakan peran yang sama bergerak bersama lewat faktor kinerja laten (rho {{num (defaultRho) 2 $l}}).{{else}}Activities done by the same role move together through a latent performance factor (rho {{num (defaultRho) 2 $l}}).{{end}}{{end}}
        {{if eq $i 2}}{{if eq $l "id"}}Risiko register terjadi dengan peluang residualnya, tetapi risiko yang berbagi sebab cenderung datang bersamaan (kopula faktor, lambda {{num (riskLoading) 1 $l}}).{{else}}Register risks fire at their residual probability, but risks sharing a cause tend to arrive together (factor copula, lambda {{num (riskLoading) 1 $l}}).{{end}}{{end}}
        {{if eq $i 3}}{{if eq $l "id"}}Regresi pasca perbaikan bug dan uji penetrasi bisa gagal lalu diulang - putaran GERT dengan jumlah ulangan geometrik.{{else}}Regression after bug fixing and the penetration test can fail and be repeated - GERT loops with a geometric number of repeats.{{end}}{{end}}
        {{if eq $i 4}}{{if eq $l "id"}}Setiap iterasi dijadwalkan ulang dengan levelling: kapasitas peran, DevOps paruh waktu, dan periode ujian dihormati.{{else}}Every iteration is rescheduled with levelling: role capacity, half-time DevOps, and the exam periods are respected.{{end}}{{end}}
      </p>
      <dl>
        <dt>P80 {{if eq $l "id"}}durasi{{else}}duration{{end}}</dt><dd>{{num $r.DurP80 0 $l}}</dd>
        <dt>P80 {{if eq $l "id"}}biaya{{else}}cost{{end}}</dt><dd>{{rpShort $r.CostP80 $l}}</dd>
        <dt>{{if eq $l "id"}}Tepat waktu{{else}}On time{{end}}</dt><dd>{{pct $r.OnTime 1 $l}}</dd>
        <dt>{{if eq $l "id"}}Tepat anggaran{{else}}On budget{{end}}</dt><dd>{{pct $r.OnBudget 1 $l}}</dd>
        <dt>JCL</dt><dd>{{pct $r.JCL 2 $l}}</dd>
      </dl>
    </article>
    {{end}}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Tangga realisme{{else}}The realism ladder{{end}}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">{{if eq $l "id"}}Kelima lapisan dijalankan dengan benih acak yang sama, sehingga selisih antar-anak tangga murni akibat efek yang ditambahkan - bukan derau sampel. Batang merentang dari P50 sampai P90; garis tebal adalah P80.{{else}}All five layers run with the same random seed, so the difference between rungs comes purely from the added effect - not from sampling noise. Bars span P50 to P90; the heavy line is P80.{{end}}</p>
  <div class="two-col">
    <figure class="figure"><div class="figure-body scrollable">{{ladderChart "dur" $l}}</div></figure>
    <figure class="figure"><div class="figure-body scrollable">{{ladderChart "cost" $l}}</div></figure>
  </div>
  <table class="data">
    <thead><tr><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Lapisan{{else}}Layer{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Rerata durasi{{else}}Mean duration{{end}}</th><th class="num">P50</th><th class="num">P80</th><th class="num">P90</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Rerata biaya{{else}}Mean cost{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}P80 biaya{{else}}P80 cost{{end}}</th><th class="num">JCL</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Bersama di P80×P80{{else}}Joint at P80×P80{{end}}</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{range $i, $r := $lad}}
      <tr class="{{if eq $i 4}}highlight{{end}}">
        <th>L{{$i}} {{tx (index $names $i) $l}}</th>
        <td class="num">{{num $r.DurMean 1 $l}}</td>
        <td class="num">{{num $r.DurP50 0 $l}}</td>
        <td class="num"><strong>{{num $r.DurP80 0 $l}}</strong></td>
        <td class="num">{{num $r.DurP90 0 $l}}</td>
        <td class="num">{{rp $r.CostMean $l}}</td>
        <td class="num"><strong>{{rp $r.CostP80 $l}}</strong></td>
        <td class="num">{{pct $r.JCL 2 $l}}</td>
        <td class="num">{{pct $r.JointAtP80 1 $l}}</td>
      </tr>
      {{end}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="note-box warn">
    <h4>{{if eq $l "id"}}Mengapa biaya di lapisan independen pun sudah di atas BAC{{else}}Why cost already exceeds BAC even in the independent layer{{end}}</h4>
    <p>{{if eq $l "id"}}BAC {{rp $a.BAC $l}} dihitung dari durasi paling mungkin (M). Tetapi estimasi tiga titik proyek ini condong ke kanan: rerata beta-PERT (O + 4M + P)/6 hampir selalu di atas M. Biaya tenaga kerja mengikuti durasi, jadi rerata biaya simulasi ({{rp (index $lad 0).CostMean $l}}) sudah di atas BAC sebelum satu risiko pun terjadi. Ini bukan kesalahan hitung - ini pengingat bahwa anggaran yang disusun dari angka "paling mungkin" secara sistematis terlalu rendah. Sewa server dan langganan tools menambah efek yang sama: setiap hari proyek melewati 85 hari, tagihannya ikut bertambah - rerata biaya sewa di L0 sudah {{rp (index $lad 0).TimeCost $l}} terhadap {{rp (index $lad 0).TimeCostPlan $l}} rencana.{{else}}BAC of {{rp $a.BAC $l}} is built from most-likely durations (M). But this project's three-point estimates skew right: the beta-PERT mean (O + 4M + P)/6 almost always sits above M. Labour cost follows duration, so the simulated mean cost ({{rp (index $lad 0).CostMean $l}}) already exceeds BAC before a single risk fires. That is not an arithmetic error - it is a reminder that a budget built from "most likely" figures is systematically too low. Server rental and tool subscriptions add the same effect: every day past 85, the bill grows - mean rental cost in L0 is already {{rp (index $lad 0).TimeCost $l}} against {{rp (index $lad 0).TimeCostPlan $l}} planned.{{end}}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Joint Confidence Level{{else}}Joint Confidence Level{{end}}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">{{if eq $l "id"}}JCL adalah peluang selesai dalam tenggat <em>dan</em> dalam anggaran sekaligus - praktik yang diwajibkan NASA untuk proyek besarnya sejak 2009, dengan ambang keyakinan 70%. Setiap sel pada peta di bawah adalah kumpulan iterasi yang berakhir pada kombinasi durasi dan biaya itu. Garis hijau adalah frontier JCL 70%: untuk setiap tenggat, anggaran minimum agar keyakinan bersamanya mencapai 70%.{{else}}JCL is the probability of finishing within the deadline <em>and</em> within budget at once - a practice NASA has required on its major projects since 2009, at a 70% confidence threshold. Each cell on the map below is the set of iterations that ended at that duration-cost combination. The green line is the 70% JCL frontier: for each deadline, the minimum budget that brings joint confidence to 70%.{{end}}</p>
  <div class="kpi-grid four">
    <div class="kpi bad"><p class="kpi-label">JCL {{if eq $l "id"}}pada target piagam{{else}}at charter target{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{pct $fin.JCL 2 $l}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{$a.Plan.Duration}} {{t $l "t.days"}} & {{rpShort (totalBudget) $l}}</p></div>
    <div class="kpi neutral"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}Peluang bersama di P80 × P80{{else}}Joint odds at P80 × P80{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{pct $fin.JointAtP80 1 $l}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{if eq $l "id"}}bukan 80% - dua P80 tidak boleh dilaporkan terpisah{{else}}not 80% - two P80s must not be reported separately{{end}}</p></div>
    <div class="kpi good"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}Komitmen JCL 70%{{else}}JCL 70% commitment{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{if $a.JCL70.Feasible}}{{num $a.JCL70.Duration 0 $l}}{{else}}—{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{if $a.JCL70.Feasible}}{{t $l "t.days"}} & {{rpShort $a.JCL70.Budget $l}}{{else}}{{if eq $l "id"}}tidak tercapai dalam rentang simulasi{{else}}not reached in the simulated range{{end}}{{end}}</p></div>
    <div class="kpi neutral"><p class="kpi-label">{{if eq $l "id"}}Iterasi{{else}}Iterations{{end}}</p><p class="kpi-value">{{num (iterf $fin.Config.Iterations) 0 $l}}</p><p class="kpi-note">{{if eq $l "id"}}benih{{else}}seed{{end}} {{$fin.Config.Seed}}</p></div>
  </div>
  <figure class="figure">
    <div class="figure-body scrollable">{{jclHeatmap $l}}</div>
  </figure>
  <div class="two-col">
    <table class="data">
      <caption>{{if eq $l "id"}}Frontier JCL 70%: tenggat terhadap anggaran minimum{{else}}JCL 70% frontier: deadline against minimum budget{{end}}</caption>
      <thead><tr><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Tenggat{{else}}Deadline{{end}}</th><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Tanggal{{else}}Date{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Anggaran minimum{{else}}Minimum budget{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Terhadap pagu{{else}}Against the cap{{end}}</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {{range frontierRows 2}}
        <tr>
          <td class="num">{{num .Duration 0 $l}}</td>
          <td class="small">{{date ($a.FinishISO (int .Duration)) $l}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{rp .Budget $l}}</td>
          <td class="num neg">{{signed (subf .Budget (totalBudget)) $l}}</td>
        </tr>
        {{end}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <figure class="figure">
      <figcaption><h3>{{if eq $l "id"}}Sebaran biaya akhir (L4){{else}}Final cost distribution (L4){{end}}</h3></figcaption>
      <div class="figure-body scrollable">{{costHistogram $l}}</div>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Seberapa peka hasilnya terhadap asumsi korelasi{{else}}How sensitive the result is to the correlation assumption{{end}}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">{{if eq $l "id"}}Nilai rho adalah asumsi, dan asumsi harus diuji, bukan dipercaya. Tabel di bawah menjalankan lapisan korelasi dengan empat nilai rho. Kolom "terealisasi" adalah rerata korelasi peringkat yang benar-benar muncul antar-aktivitas dengan peran sama - bukti bahwa model kopulanya bekerja seperti yang diklaim.{{else}}Rho is an assumption, and assumptions must be tested rather than trusted. The table below runs the correlation layer at four rho values. The "realised" column is the mean rank correlation that actually appears between same-role activities - evidence that the copula model works as claimed.{{end}}</p>
  <table class="data">
    <thead><tr><th class="num">rho</th><th class="num">P80 {{if eq $l "id"}}durasi{{else}}duration{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Simpangan baku{{else}}Std. deviation{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Tepat waktu{{else}}On time{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Korelasi terealisasi{{else}}Realised correlation{{end}}</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{range $a.RhoSweep}}
      <tr class="{{if eq .Rho (defaultRho)}}highlight{{end}}">
        <td class="num">{{num .Rho 2 $l}}</td>
        <td class="num">{{num .P80 0 $l}}</td>
        <td class="num">{{num .StdDev 2 $l}}</td>
        <td class="num">{{pct .OnTime 2 $l}}</td>
        <td class="num">{{num .Realised 3 $l}}</td>
      </tr>
      {{end}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="note-box">
    <p>{{if eq $l "id"}}Korelasi melebarkan sebaran ke dua arah sekaligus. Itulah sebabnya peluang tepat waktu justru naik sedikit saat rho dinaikkan: ekor kiri ikut memanjang. Yang berubah berarti bukan P80 - yang hanya bergeser satu hari - melainkan lebar sebarannya. Kesimpulan halaman ini tidak bergantung pada rho: bahkan dengan rho nol, lapisan risiko dan kapasitas saja sudah mendorong P80 jauh melewati 17 minggu.{{else}}Correlation widens the spread in both directions at once. That is why the on-time probability actually rises slightly as rho increases: the left tail lengthens too. What changes materially is not P80 - which moves just one day - but the width of the spread. This page's conclusion does not hinge on rho: even at rho zero, the risk and capacity layers alone push P80 far past 17 weeks.{{end}}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" data-wasm-panel hidden>
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Jalankan simulasi terpadu di peramban{{else}}Run the integrated simulation in your browser{{end}}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">{{if eq $l "id"}}Mesin Go yang sama, dikompilasi ke WebAssembly. Geser rho, pilih sampai lapisan mana simulasi dijalankan, lalu lihat JCL berubah. Lapisan kapasitas menjadwalkan ulang setiap iterasi, jadi jalankan dengan iterasi lebih sedikit di perangkat yang lambat.{{else}}The same Go engine, compiled to WebAssembly. Move rho, choose how many layers to run, and watch the JCL change. The capacity layer reschedules every iteration, so use fewer iterations on a slow device.{{end}}</p>
  <form class="sim-form int-form" data-int-form>
    <label><span>rho</span>
      <span><input type="range" name="rho" min="0" max="0.9" step="0.05" value="{{defaultRho}}"> <output data-rho-out>{{num (defaultRho) 2 $l}}</output></span>
    </label>
    <label><span>{{if eq $l "id"}}Sampai lapisan{{else}}Up to layer{{end}}</span>
      <select name="layer">
        {{range $i, $n := $names}}<option value="{{$i}}"{{if eq $i 4}} selected{{end}}>L{{$i}} {{tx $n $l}}</option>{{end}}
      </select>
    </label>
    <label><span>{{if eq $l "id"}}Iterasi{{else}}Iterations{{end}}</span>
      <select name="iterations">
        <option value="1000">1.000</option>
        <option value="3000" selected>3.000</option>
        <option value="5000">5.000</option>
      </select>
    </label>
    <button type="submit">{{if eq $l "id"}}Jalankan{{else}}Run{{end}}</button>
  </form>
  <div class="live-out sim-out">
    <div><span>JCL</span><strong data-int="jcl">—</strong></div>
    <div><span>{{if eq $l "id"}}Tepat waktu{{else}}On time{{end}}</span><strong data-int="onTime">—</strong></div>
    <div><span>{{if eq $l "id"}}Tepat anggaran{{else}}On budget{{end}}</span><strong data-int="onBudget">—</strong></div>
    <div><span>P80 {{if eq $l "id"}}durasi{{else}}duration{{end}}</span><strong data-int="durP80">—</strong></div>
    <div><span>P80 {{if eq $l "id"}}biaya{{else}}cost{{end}}</span><strong data-int="costP80">—</strong></div>
    <div><span>{{if eq $l "id"}}Korelasi terealisasi{{else}}Realised correlation{{end}}</span><strong data-int="realised">—</strong></div>
    <div><span>{{if eq $l "id"}}Waktu hitung{{else}}Compute time{{end}}</span><strong data-int="elapsed">—</strong></div>
  </div>
  <div class="figure-body scrollable" data-int-chart></div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Risiko yang datang bergerombol{{else}}Risks that arrive together{{end}}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">{{if eq $l "id"}}Versi sebelumnya melempar koin terpisah untuk setiap risiko. Padahal kolom "penyebab" pada register menunjukkan beberapa risiko lahir dari sebab yang sama. Setiap penggerak di bawah punya satu faktor laten per iterasi; risiko pada penggerak itu terjadi bila Φ(λ·Z + √(1−λ²)·ε) &gt; 1 − p. Peluang marginal setiap risiko tetap persis p - jadi EMV dan rerata biaya tidak berubah - tetapi skenario "semuanya salah bersamaan" menjadi sesering kenyataannya. Penggerak kinerja pengembang memakai faktor laten Backend Developer yang sama dengan sampler durasi, sehingga risiko R02 juga berkorelasi dengan lamanya API dikerjakan.{{else}}The previous version flipped a separate coin for every risk. Yet the register's "cause" column shows several risks stem from the same cause. Each driver below has one latent factor per iteration; a risk on that driver fires when Φ(λ·Z + √(1−λ²)·ε) &gt; 1 − p. Each risk's marginal probability stays exactly p - so EMV and mean cost do not change - but the "everything goes wrong together" scenario becomes as frequent as it really is. The development-performance driver uses the same Backend Developer latent factor as the duration sampler, so R02 also correlates with how long the APIs take.{{end}}</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table class="data">
    <thead><tr><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Penggerak bersama{{else}}Shared driver{{end}}</th><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Risiko{{else}}Risks{{end}}</th><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Dasar pengelompokan{{else}}Grouping rationale{{end}}</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{range riskDrivers}}
      <tr>
        <th>{{tx .Label $l}}{{if .Role}} <span class="pill neutral">{{if eq $l "id"}}faktor{{else}}factor{{end}} {{.Role}}</span>{{end}}</th>
        <td>{{range $i, $id := risksOfDriver .Key}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}<code>{{$id}}</code>{{end}}</td>
        <td class="small">{{tx .Why $l}}</td>
      </tr>
      {{end}}
      <tr class="muted"><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Tanpa penggerak{{else}}No driver{{end}}</th><td><code>R01</code></td><td class="small">{{if eq $l "id"}}Keengganan alumni mengisi kuesioner adalah perilaku pihak luar tanpa sebab bersama dengan risiko lain.{{else}}Alumni reluctance to answer is outside behaviour with no cause shared by other risks.{{end}}</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data">
      <caption>{{if eq $l "id"}}Kepekaan terhadap lambda (lapisan L2){{else}}Sensitivity to lambda (layer L2){{end}}</caption>
      <thead><tr><th class="num">lambda</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}phi terealisasi{{else}}realised phi{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Rerata biaya{{else}}Mean cost{{end}}</th><th class="num">P95 {{if eq $l "id"}}biaya{{else}}cost{{end}}</th><th class="num">P95 {{if eq $l "id"}}durasi{{else}}duration{{end}}</th><th class="num">≥ {{manyRisks}} {{if eq $l "id"}}risiko{{else}}risks{{end}}</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {{range $a.RiskSweep}}
        <tr class="{{if eq .Loading (riskLoading)}}highlight{{end}}">
          <td class="num">{{num .Loading 1 $l}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{num .Phi 3 $l}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{rp .CostMean $l}}</td>
          <td class="num"><strong>{{rp .CostP95 $l}}</strong></td>
          <td class="num">{{num .DurP95 0 $l}}</td>
          <td class="num">{{pct .ManyRisks 1 $l}}</td>
        </tr>
        {{end}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <figure class="figure"><div class="figure-body scrollable">{{riskCountBars $l}}</div></figure>
  <div class="note-box">
    <p>{{if eq $l "id"}}Perhatikan kolom rerata biaya: praktis sama di setiap baris. Kopula tidak menambah risiko, ia hanya menata ulang KAPAN risiko terjadi. Yang berubah adalah ekor - P95 biaya dan durasi - dan itulah angka yang menentukan apakah cadangan cukup pada tahun yang buruk.{{else}}Look at the mean cost column: practically identical in every row. The copula adds no risk; it only rearranges WHEN risks fire. What changes is the tail - P95 cost and duration - and that is the figure that decides whether the reserve survives a bad year.{{end}}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Putaran rework: GERT{{else}}Rework loops: GERT{{end}}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">{{if eq $l "id"}}Modul 4 menyebut GERT untuk kegiatan yang tidak berurutan lurus, "seperti loop (tes yang harus diulang lebih dari sekali)". Jaringan CPM wajib asiklis, jadi putaran tidak bisa digambar di sana. GERT memberi setiap cabang peluang: pemeriksaan lulus dengan peluang 1 − p, atau gagal dengan peluang p lalu kembali memperbaiki. Transmitansi W(s) = p·e^(st) direduksi dengan aturan Mason W_E = W_maju / (1 − W_putar), dan momen waktunya dibaca dari turunan fungsi pembangkit momen di s = 0. Bentuk tertutupnya: rerata tambahan p·r/(1−p), simpangan baku √p·r/(1−p). Kolom Monte Carlo adalah bukti silang dari lapisan L3.{{else}}Module 4 names GERT for activities that do not run in a straight line, "such as loops (tests that must be repeated more than once)". A CPM network must be acyclic, so loops cannot be drawn there. GERT gives every branch a probability: a check passes with probability 1 − p, or fails with probability p and returns to fixing. The transmittance W(s) = p·e^(st) is reduced with Mason's rule W_E = W_forward / (1 − W_loop), and the time moments are read from derivatives of the moment generating function at s = 0. Closed form: mean extra p·r/(1−p), standard deviation √p·r/(1−p). The Monte Carlo column is the cross-check from layer L3.{{end}}</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table class="data">
    <thead><tr><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Putaran{{else}}Loop{{end}}</th><th class="num">p</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Hari per putaran{{else}}Days per loop{{end}}</th><th class="num">E[N] {{if eq $l "id"}}analitik{{else}}analytic{{end}}</th><th class="num">E[N] Monte Carlo</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Rerata tambahan{{else}}Mean extra{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Simpangan baku{{else}}Std. deviation{{end}}</th><th class="num">P(N ≥ 2)</th><th class="num">N {{if eq $l "id"}}pada 90%{{else}}at 90%{{end}}</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{range $a.GERT}}
      <tr>
        <th><code>{{.Loop.ID}}</code> {{tx .Loop.Label $l}} <span class="small muted">({{if eq $l "id"}}pemeriksaan{{else}}check{{end}} {{.Loop.Check}})</span></th>
        <td class="num">{{pct .Loop.FailProb 0 $l}}</td>
        <td class="num">{{num .ReworkDays 2 $l}}</td>
        <td class="num">{{num .Cycles 3 $l}}</td>
        <td class="num">{{num .MCCycles 3 $l}}</td>
        <td class="num"><strong>{{num .Reduced.Mean 2 $l}}</strong></td>
        <td class="num">{{num .Reduced.SD 2 $l}}</td>
        <td class="num">{{pct .AtLeastTwo 1 $l}}</td>
        <td class="num">{{.Q90}}</td>
      </tr>
      {{end}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  <div class="two-col">
    {{range $a.GERT}}
    <div class="note-box">
      <h4><code>{{.Loop.ID}}</code> {{tx .Loop.Label $l}} <span class="pill warn">{{if eq $l "id"}}peluang asumsi{{else}}assumed probability{{end}}</span></h4>
      <p class="small">{{tx .Loop.Why $l}}</p>
    </div>
    {{end}}
  </div>
  <p class="small muted">{{if eq $l "id"}}Rerata hari tambahan di simulasi ({{num (index $lad 3).ReworkDays 2 $l}} hari) sedikit di atas jumlah analitik karena simulasi memakai durasi sampel, yang reratanya (O + 4M + P)/6 di atas M yang dipakai bentuk tertutup.{{else}}The simulated mean extra days ({{num (index $lad 3).ReworkDays 2 $l}}) sit slightly above the analytic sum because the simulation uses sampled durations, whose mean (O + 4M + P)/6 exceeds the M used by the closed form.{{end}}</p>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Biaya yang bergantung waktu{{else}}Time-dependent cost{{end}}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">{{if eq $l "id"}}Anggaran bottom-up memuat dua jenis biaya non-tenaga-kerja. Pembelian sekali - hosting produksi setahun, pelatihan - tidak peduli proyek selesai kapan. Sewa dan langganan berbeda: nilainya pada anggaran adalah nilai untuk rentang rencana, dan setiap hari proyek molor tagihannya bertambah. Pada jadwal CPM rencana biayanya persis sama dengan BAC; di setiap iterasi simulasi, rentangnya mengikuti jadwal iterasi itu.{{else}}The bottom-up budget holds two kinds of non-labour cost. One-off purchases - a year of production hosting, training - do not care when the project finishes. Rentals and subscriptions differ: their budget value covers the planned span, and every day the project slips the bill grows. On the planned CPM schedule the cost equals BAC exactly; in every simulation iteration the span follows that iteration's schedule.{{end}}</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table class="data">
    <thead><tr><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Pos biaya{{else}}Cost item{{end}}</th><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Dibeli pada{{else}}Bought at{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Nilai rencana{{else}}Planned value{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Rentang rencana{{else}}Planned span{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Tarif per hari{{else}}Rate per day{{end}}</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{range $a.Rentals}}
      <tr><th>{{tx .Label $l}}</th><td><code>{{.Activity}}</code></td><td class="num">{{rp .Amount $l}}</td><td class="num">{{.PlanSpan}} {{t $l "t.days"}}</td><td class="num">{{rp .Rate $l}}</td></tr>
      {{end}}
      <tr class="highlight"><th colspan="4">{{if eq $l "id"}}Tambahan per hari keterlambatan{{else}}Extra per day of delay{{end}}</th><td class="num"><strong>{{rp $a.RentalDaily $l}}</strong></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  <p class="small">{{if eq $l "id"}}Rerata biaya sewa per lapisan: {{range $i, $r := $lad}}{{if $i}} → {{end}}L{{$i}} {{rpShort $r.TimeCost $l}}{{end}}. Lapisan kapasitas paling mahal karena jadwal yang menghormati kapasitas selalu lebih panjang - biaya itu tidak pernah terlihat di BAC.{{else}}Mean rental cost per layer: {{range $i, $r := $lad}}{{if $i}} → {{end}}L{{$i}} {{rpShort $r.TimeCost $l}}{{end}}. The capacity layer is the most expensive because a schedule that respects capacity is always longer - a cost BAC never shows.{{end}}</p>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2>{{if eq $l "id"}}Frekuensi kejadian risiko di simulasi{{else}}Risk event frequency in the simulation{{end}}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">{{if eq $l "id"}}Bila terjadi, dampak rupiah risiko ditambahkan ke biaya, dan dampak jadwalnya ditambahkan ke aktivitas terpanjang pada paket kerja risiko itu - atau ke aktivitas terakhir bila risikonya lintas fase. Karena kopula menjaga peluang marginal, frekuensi di bawah tetap bisa dicocokkan dengan peluang residual pada halaman Risiko.{{else}}When a risk fires, its monetary impact is added to cost and its schedule impact to the longest activity in its work package - or to the final activity for cross-phase risks. Because the copula preserves marginal probabilities, the frequencies below still match the residual probabilities on the Risk page.{{end}}</p>
  <table class="data">
    <thead><tr><th>{{t $l "t.code"}}</th><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Risiko{{else}}Risk{{end}}</th><th>{{if eq $l "id"}}Penggerak{{else}}Driver{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Peluang residual{{else}}Residual probability{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Frekuensi di simulasi{{else}}Simulated frequency{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Dampak biaya{{else}}Cost impact{{end}}</th><th class="num">{{if eq $l "id"}}Dampak jadwal{{else}}Schedule impact{{end}}</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{range risks}}
      <tr>
        <td><code>{{.ID}}</code></td>
        <td>{{tx .Title $l}}</td>
        <td class="small">{{with driverOf .}}{{driverLabel . $l}}{{else}}—{{end}}</td>
        <td class="num">{{pct .ResidualProb 0 $l}}</td>
        <td class="num">{{pct (div (iterf (index $fin.RiskHits .ID)) (iterf $fin.Config.Iterations)) 1 $l}}</td>
        <td class="num">{{rp .ResidualImpact $l}}</td>
        <td class="num">{{if .ScheduleImpact}}+{{.ScheduleImpact}} {{if eq $l "id"}}hari{{else}}days{{end}}{{if eq .ID "R08"}} <span class="pill warn">{{if eq $l "id"}}di L4 via kalender{{else}}in L4 via calendar{{end}}</span>{{end}}{{else}}—{{end}}</td>
      </tr>
      {{end}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>
{{end}}
